@@ -10,6 +10,25 @@ sidebarTitle: "Gateway and nodes"
 
 Reach the Gateway and paired nodes from plugin code, and the events a long-lived Gateway service receives. Part of the [Plugin runtime helpers](/plugins/sdk-runtime) reference.
 
+## CLI response limits
+
+Import `callGatewayFromCli` from
+`openclaw/plugin-sdk/gateway-runtime` when a CLI read needs an explicit complete,
+decompressed WebSocket message limit. Require `callGatewayFromCli.responseLimitVersion === 1` before opting in; older
+SDKs can silently ignore unknown extra options. Its fourth argument accepts
+`maxPayloadBytes`: positive safe integers from 1 through 67,108,864 select a
+finite cap. Ordinary `callGatewayFromCli` calls retain the 26,214,400-byte default.
+
+Zero explicitly removes the receive cap. The call owner admits zero only for
+the configured local Gateway at a numeric loopback address, with shared token
+or password authentication and without a URL override or SSH tunnel. Remote
+mode and missing shared authentication are rejected before dispatch. This does
+not change scopes, authentication requirements, deadlines or retry policy.
+Only opt in for a trusted complete read whose resource admission is owned by
+the caller. Uncapped messages can consume unbounded memory, and parsing and
+concurrent reads add overhead; deadlines do not bound peak memory. Prefer
+supported pagination when the server contract offers it.
+
